arbon ratios and SdO-derived features, enhancing biodegradability association.\ndf['cross_combined_C_O_with_ratio_SdO_nO'] = df['combined_C_O_C_ratio'] * df['ratio_SdO_nO']", "# zscore_SdO\n# Z-score normalization of SdO to center and scale values.\n# Usefulness: Standardizes the oxygen bonding feature for easier integration into machine learning models.\ndf['zscore_SdO'] = (df['SdO'] - df['SdO'].mean()) / df['SdO'].std()", "# rolling_mean_nCp\n# Rolling mean of nCp over a window of 5 to capture local patterns in terminal primary C(sp3).\n# Usefulness: Emphasizes short-term trends in carbon configuration that may contribute to biodegradability prediction.\ndf['rolling_mean_nCp'] = df['nCp'].rolling(window=5, min_periods=1).mean()", "# cumulative_nX\n# Cumulative sum of nX to monitor progressive influence of halogens across data points.\n# Usefulness: Aggregates halogen atom counts, crucial for understanding halogen impact over the dataset.\ndf['cumulative_nX'] = df['nX'].cumsum()", "# square_Psi_i_A\n# Square transformation of Psi_i_A for higher-order modeling of intrinsic state connectivity.\n# Usefulness: Highlights quadratic effects of intrinsic connectivity states linked to structural properties.\ndf['square_Psi_i_A'] = df['Psi_i_A']  2", "# reciprocal_nArNO2\n# Reciprocal transformation of nArNO2+1 for diminishing impact of outliers.\n# Usefulness: Addresses sparsity of nitro group count while retaining meaningful influence on biodegradability.\ndf['reciprocal_nArNO2'] = 1 / (df['nArNO2'] + 1)", "# abs_SdssC\n# Absolute value of SdssC to focus on magnitude rather than sign of bonding environment E-states for carbon.\n# Usefulness: Magnitude provides additional insight into bonding environments without directional bias.\ndf['abs_SdssC'] = df['SdssC'].abs()", "df.drop(columns=['F02[C-N]', 'F03C_O_F02C_N_ratio'], inplace=True)"]
