_SpMax_B_Psi to ensure focus on magnitude rather than direction of molecular connectivity dynamics.\n# Usefulness: Reflects intensity of connectivity-related patterns relevant for biodegradation.\n\ndf['abs_interaction_SpMax_B_Psi'] = df['interaction_SpMax_B_Psi'].abs()", "# drop_nN_N_nArCOOR\n# Drop columns that have limited variance (e.g., mostly 0s) and provide limited predictive power for biodegradability.\ndf.drop(columns=['nN-N', 'nArCOOR'], inplace=True)", "# exp_inverse_combined_C_O_C_ratio\n# Exponential transformation applied to the reciprocal of combined_C_O_C_ratio to capture nonlinear effects of chemical composition.\n# Usefulness: Highlights nonlinear reduction patterns in complex compositional attributes that may affect molecular degradation.\n\ndf['exp_inverse_combined_C_O_C_ratio'] = np.exp(1 / df['combined_C_O_C_ratio'])", "# rank_interaction_nCp_log_C_percent_Sorted\n# Rank interaction_nCp_log_C_percent values in ascending order to standardize their importance rankings across molecules.\n# Usefulness: Provides relative importance ranking for primary carbon-carbon composition interactions on biodegradability.\n\ndf['rank_interaction_nCp_log_C_percent_Sorted'] = df['interaction_nCp_log_C_percent'].rank()"]
